<final_code>
```python
def test_timer_context_manager_restart_raises_error():
    """Test that Timer context manager properly handles start/stop and raises TimerError on restart without stopping."""
    # Create a Timer instance
    timer_instance = timer.Timer()
    
    # Use the timer as a context manager (__enter__ starts it)
    returned_from_enter = timer_instance.__enter__()
    
    # Exit the context manager (__exit__ stops it)
    exit_result = timer_instance.__exit__()
    
    # Start the timer again via the instance returned from __enter__
    second_start_result = returned_from_enter.start()
    
    # Attempt to start an already-running timer - expected to raise TimerError
    timer_instance.start()
```
</final_code>
